  "metaTitle": "Dockless Bike / E-Scooter Accident Attorney",
  "metaDescription": "Injured in a dockless bike or scooter accident? A Denver Dockless Bike/Scooter Accident Lawyer can help. Get your free consultation today!",
  "body": [
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bby8",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "lby5",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sby4",
          "text": "At Dormer Harpring, our ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sby6",
          "text": "Denver personal injury lawyers",
          "marks": [
            "lby5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sby7",
          "text": " have experience representing victims of injuries related to dockless vehicles, including bikes and e-scooters, in Colorado. Learn more about dockless rental vehicles here and contact us today to discuss your injury case in a free consultation.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bbya",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sby9",
          "text": "What is a “Dockless Vehicle”?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bbyc",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sbyb",
          "text": "You may have noticed brightly colored bikes with front-mounted baskets, or all-black or bright green-and-white electric scooters, rolling around Denver, parked in the street, blocking sidewalks, and appearing in large numbers downtown. These bikes and scooters can be rented on smartphone apps, picked up from any location, and dropped off or parked at any location according to local county, city, and company rules.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bbyk",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "lbye",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://www.citylab.com/city-makers-connections/bike-share/"
        },
        {
          "_key": "lbyh",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://www.citylab.com/transportation/2018/04/a-complete-taxonomy-of-bikeshare-so-far/558560/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sbyd",
          "text": "This term came into existence as the opposite of “docked” vehicles, which have existed in many large cities across the globe for many years, dating back even to the ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sbyf",
          "text": "1960’s",
          "marks": [
            "lbye"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sbyg",
          "text": ". These docked vehicles began as bike-shares where a customer could come to a bike station, rent a bike, and then bike to another docking station to check the bike back in. These programs became popular in Europe in the 1990’s and eventually spread throughout many American cities in the 2000’s, including our local version in Denver, “B-Cycle.” ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sbyi",
          "text": "In the past couple years",
          "marks": [
            "lbyh"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sbyj",
          "text": ", tech companies have rolled out “dockless” bikes through smartphone apps, and these companies have aggressively forced their way into many metropolitan areas. In Denver, this disruption began in June of 2018, and by the end of July, the City had shifted its position from an outright ban to permission by-permit.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bbym",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sbyl",
          "text": "Operators of these products in Colorado include:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
